[2026-08-21T11:25:49+00:00] pi-student ultra: ok=False leak=True exit=0 actual='The tzip skill was invoked with "Hi" (other text). According to its Usage section, when a skill is invoked with any other text, I should pass it as CLI parameters to `example.sh` and report the output. However, looking at the tzip skill\'s specific instructions:\n\n- Modes: `tzip`, `tzip on`, `tzip lite`, `tzip full`, `tzip ultra`, `tzip off`\n- Communication pattern: `<thing> [action] [reason]`\n- Reply with mode name (e.g., "tzip lite activated", "tzip deactivated")\n\nThe script was called and returned `ultra`. Following the skill\'s instruction to reply with a mode name, I should respond accordingly.\n\n**tzip ultra activated**' thinking_len=9115
[2026-08-21T11:26:03+00:00] pi-student off: ok=False leak=True exit=0 actual='The skill system is working as designed. Here\'s a quick recap of what happened:\n\n**Available skills** (from the initial list):\n- **git** – Git version control\n- **skman** – Agent Skills System scaffolding & validation\n- **webfetch** – Fetch web pages to LLM-ready markdown\n- **websearch** – Search DuckDuckGo with LLM-optimized output\n- **find-skills** – Discover and install agent skills\n- **tzip** – Token-pruning communication mode (default: `lite`)\n- **example** – Minimal skill demonstrating the format\n\n**How it works:**\n- Each skill has a `SKILL.md` with frontmatter metadata, body content, helper scripts in `scripts/`, and reference files.\n- When invoked:\n  - **No extra text** → reply exactly as specified (e.g., "This is an example skill.")\n  - **"Hello"** → load the relevant reference file (e.g., `03-hello.md`) and follow its instructions\n  - **Any other text / "call script"** → pass the user\'s text to a helper script in `scripts/` and report the output\n\n**Recent actions:**\n- Invoked `example` with no text → replied exactly `This is an example skill.`\n- Invoked `example` with "Hello" → ran `scripts/example.sh Hello` → got `world`\n- Invoked `tzip` (default mode) → activated token pruning, then deactivated it (`off`) when called\n\nThe tzip skill was activated by default and immediately deactivated after the call. The system is fully operational. Is there anything specific you\'d like to explore further?' thinking_len=1824
